TASK-195 runtime harness: a Private window's content-blocking switch is kept
in memory only. Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Needs:

    SP=<scratch>; mkdir -p $SP/www $SP/out
    # www/page.html: <script>window.__loaded=false</script>
    #                <script src="/jquery.popunder.js"></script>
    # www/jquery.popunder.js: window.__loaded = true;
    # EasyList blocks `/jquery.popunder.js` on any host.
    python3 -m http.server 8895 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory $SP/www &
    # A v18 data dir: DetourVerify182's v17 browser.db with v18 applied by hand
    # in sqlite3 (create siteSetting, copy/drop contentBlockerWhitelist, add the
    # 'v18' grdb_migrations row), its ContentBlocker and ContentRuleLists dirs
    # copied, and seeded rows: Private seeded.test contentBlocking 0, Private
    # youtube.com pictureInPicture 0, Default normal-seeded.test contentBlocking 0.
    git apply docs/harness/task195-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify195 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR=$SP/out DETOUR_VERIFY_PORT=8895 \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber>": screencapture -x -o -l <windowNumber>;
    # wait for "done" (about 32 s), kill that pid and the server.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task195-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

The page is loaded from http://lvh.me:8895 (public DNS for 127.0.0.1), not
127.0.0.1 or localhost: EasyList's `@@://127.0.0.1$generichide` and
`@@://localhost:$generichide` compile (EasyListParser) to a plain
ignore-previous-rules, so nothing on those hosts is ever blocked. Not
http://[::1] either: an IPv6-literal URL crashes BrowserTab's optimistic
favicon URL (force unwrap of URL(string: "http://::1/favicon.ico")).

Steps: baseline in the normal window; open a Private window, switch blocking
off through the site popover (performClick), back on, off again; reload the
normal window's tab, switch it off there; close the Private window, open a new
one. Probes read window.__loaded and the tab's blockedCount.

Results (2026-10-24):
- v18 -> v19 at launch: the Private seeded.test contentBlocking row was gone,
  the Private pictureInPicture row and the Default profile's row stayed.
- Baseline, normal window: script blocked (blockedCount 1).
- Private window before: blocked. Switch off: whitelisted in memory, 0 rows
  in browser.db, the page reloaded and the script loaded (blockedCount 0).
  Switch back on: in-memory override empty, reloaded, blocked again. Off again:
  loads, still 0 rows.
- Normal window (reloaded) while the Private switch was off: still blocked.
  Switch off there: 1 row (Default lvh.me contentBlocking false), script loads.
- Last Private window closed: no Private space, in-memory overrides empty.
  New Private window: blocked (blockedCount 1), popover switch on.

